s it to the view and the view  sends it back to the action and that's  exactly how the steps would continue in  sequence so when we trigger an action  the dispatcher will get notified once  the dispatcher has dealt with an action  the stores listening to it will get  triggered the view gets updated when the  state of the store changes user action  at the view is sent to the dispatcher to  then be processed how is redux different  from flux redux is an open source  javascript library used to manage  application state the store state is  immutable it can only have a single  store and it uses the concept of reducer  flux on the other hand is an  architecture and not a framework or  library the store state is mutable it  can have multiple stores and it uses the  concept of dispatcher let's look at some  react router questions what is a react  router a react router is a package which  is used to create routing in a react  application react router is used for  developing single page web applications  it allows multiple views in a single  application by defining multiple routes  in that react application how is react  routing different from conventional  routing react routing has a single html  page it uses or the end user rather  would navigate multiple views within the  same file called a single page app the  page does not refresh since it's a  single page file and there is improved  performance since you are not navigating  across multiple pages conventional  routing each view is a separate html  file the user would navigate multiple  files for each view the page would  refresh every time the user navigates  which would hence result in slower  performance how do you implement react  routing you can implement react routing  using a very simple method considering  the above components let's say you've  got a component called app about and  contact so here you can specify the  route path if the route part is just  slash the route defaults out it takes  you to the app component if the route is  slash about in the url given by the end  user you automatically navigate and  activate and load the about component  and if the url is slash contact it would  take you to the contact component let's  talk about react styling questions how  do you style react components either you  use inline styling by using simple css  by simply saying color blue and that's  going to be the output of the h1 element  or i could use a javascript object by  specifying a constant simple style  object and specifying a keypair value of  color background color margin font  family and apply that object as the  style parameter which would result in  this styled output how do you style  react components using a css style sheet  so here's an external style sheet so  we've written all the styling rules in a  separate css file app.css we've imported  that at the top of the app.js react  class and lo and behold you have the  output simplified as generated on your  page let's explain the use of css  modules in react so a css module file is  created.module.css  is the extension the css inside a module  file is available only for the component  that is importing it so there are no  naming conflicts so dot button is the  css styling inside button.module.css  and that is what we've imported from in  the app.js file so when you view the  button style start button is the styling  picked up from the button.module.css  file and so with that we come to the end  of this full course video i hope you  found this video interesting thank you  so much for being here keep learning and  stay tuned to simply learn  you
 

